  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(0,\\pi )\\times ((0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =((0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\cup ((0,\\pi )\\times (\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}y\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}\u2061y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
